arm64: dts: h713: the HY300 Pro's display firmware elog addresses

Its image keeps the event log 0xC00 below the HY310's: the mode-1 ring at
0x4b27219c and the control block at 0x4b48b200, whose pointer group is the
0x4b48b6a4.. that this board's own elog_mode1_ring100k_write writes (buffer
base 0x8b27219c, write 0x8b48b6a8, read 0x8b48b6a4, overflow 0x8b48b6a1,
enable 0x8b48b6ac in MIPS view; analysis A12, 18.09.2026,
umbau/reviews/A12.md). The HY310's are 0x8b272d9c and 0x8b48c2a8/a4/a1/ac.

cpu_comm reads those two addresses (patch 0092a); on this board it has been
reading the HY310's and dumping an empty ring - "0 lines" - which reads like
a dead coprocessor and is not one.

Tested on the HY310: no change. The property is in this board's file only,
and cpu_comm falls back to its built-in HY310 defaults when it is absent.
The HY300 Pro's owner boots the next TEST image with it.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
@@ -34,3 +34,14 @@
 &backlight {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
+
+/*
+ * This board's display firmware keeps its event log 0xC00 below the HY310's:
+ * the mode-1 ring at 0x4b27219c and the control block at 0x4b48b200, whose
+ * pointer group is the 0x4b48b6a4.. that its own elog_mode1_ring100k_write
+ * uses (analysis A12, 18.09.2026). Without this, cpu_comm reads the HY310's
+ * addresses, finds DRAM that holds nothing, and prints an empty dump.
+ */
+&cpu_comm {
+	allwinner,elog = <0x4b48b200 0x4b27219c>;
+};
